Feature: MCP Server Adapter
  As a specialist agent user interacting via Claude Desktop
  I want the agent to expose role-specific tools over the MCP protocol
  So that I can invoke agent capabilities from Claude Desktop without CLI knowledge

  Background:
    Given a valid role configuration exists for the role under test
    And the role configuration includes a fleet.tools section

  # ━━ GROUP A: Key Examples ━━

  # Why: Core path — the MCP server reads tool definitions from role.yaml and exposes them
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Starting an MCP server exposes tools defined in role.yaml
    Given the "architect" role defines 3 tools in its fleet.tools section
    When the MCP server starts with role "architect"
    Then the server should expose exactly 3 MCP tools
    And each tool name should match the fleet.tools definitions

  # Why: Proves the adapter is role-agnostic — same binary, different tools per role
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Different roles expose different MCP tools
    Given the "architect" role defines tools including "run_architecture_session"
    And the "product-owner" role defines tools including "run_product_session"
    When an MCP server starts with role "architect"
    Then the tool "run_architecture_session" should be available
    And the tool "run_product_session" should not be available

  # Why: End-to-end path — an MCP tool call reaches the core API
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Invoking an MCP tool delegates to the core API
    Given the MCP server is running with role "architect"
    When the "run_architecture_session" tool is called with valid parameters
